### into_iter

<!-- livebook:{"chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.Spiral.Kino.SmartCell","attrs":{"timeout":300,"source":"// Native Rust maps the rayon pipeline (into_par_iter / par_map / par_collect) to a sequential map over an array: its\n// elements (`Rc<str>`, `Rc<dyn Fn>`) and the closures' captured trace state are not `Send`. Every stage is a plain\n// Spiral array: Fable's rayon types (`IntoIter`, and `Map` with its source stage as a phantom parameter) and the\n// type-level backend switches that chose them are gone.\ntype into_iter t = array_base t","print_code":false},"livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Spiral.Kino.eval!(
  ~S"""
  // Native Rust maps the rayon pipeline (into_par_iter / par_map / par_collect) to a sequential map over an array: its
  // elements (`Rc<str>`, `Rc<dyn Fn>`) and the closures' captured trace state are not `Send`. Every stage is a plain
  // Spiral array: Fable's rayon types (`IntoIter`, and `Map` with its source stage as a phantom parameter) and the
  // type-level backend switches that chose them are gone.
  type into_iter t = array_base t
  """,
  timeout: 300_000
)
```

### into_par_iter

<!-- livebook:{"chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.Spiral.Kino.SmartCell","attrs":{"timeout":300,"source":"inl into_par_iter forall t. (x : am'.vec t) : into_iter t =\n    x |> am'.from_vec_base","print_code":false},"livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Spiral.Kino.eval!(
  ~S"""
  inl into_par_iter forall t. (x : am'.vec t) : into_iter t =
      x |> am'.from_vec_base
  """,
  timeout: 300_000
)
```

### par_map

<!-- livebook:{"chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.Spiral.Kino.SmartCell","attrs":{"timeout":300,"source":"inl par_map forall t u. (fn : t -> u) (ar : into_iter t) : into_iter u =\n    // Spiral's own map: a closure over a tuple takes its fields as separate parameters, which an emitted\n    // `|x| f(x)` can't spread.\n    // Pushed in order: a new array would be filled with `Default::default()`, which `Result` and others lack.\n    inl n : i32 = $'(!ar.borrow().len() as i32)'\n    let rec loop (i : i32) (acc : am'.vec u) : am'.vec u =\n        if i < n then loop (i + 1) (acc |> am'.vec_push (fn (am'.index_base i ar))) else acc\n    loop 0 (am'.new_vec []) |> am'.from_vec_base","print_code":false},"livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Spiral.Kino.eval!(
  ~S"""
  inl par_map forall t u. (fn : t -> u) (ar : into_iter t) : into_iter u =
      // Spiral's own map: a closure over a tuple takes its fields as separate parameters, which an emitted
      // `|x| f(x)` can't spread.
      // Pushed in order: a new array would be filled with `Default::default()`, which `Result` and others lack.
      inl n : i32 = $'(!ar.borrow().len() as i32)'
      let rec loop (i : i32) (acc : am'.vec u) : am'.vec u =
          if i < n then loop (i + 1) (acc |> am'.vec_push (fn (am'.index_base i ar))) else acc
      loop 0 (am'.new_vec []) |> am'.from_vec_base
  """,
  timeout: 300_000
)
```

